appears some changes are coming to the  embattled Clark County School Board  three incumbents running but only one  may survive Mary Jane beliesza live this  afternoon at District headquarters with  the details Mary Jane  a change to the board is on the way for  the Clark County School District as  voters got a chance to set the course  for the country's largest fifth largest  school district on Tuesday there are  three board seats up for grabs and  District D president Irene Cepeda is  running against Brenda Zamora Cepeda was  elected to the board in 2018 and took  over as president in early 2022 after  serving as vice president meanwhile in  District F trustee Danielle Ford is  running against Irene Bustamante Adams  trustee Linda Cavazos and former Eureka  County school superintendent Greg weeman  are competing for the district G seat  this election follows years of turmoil  as the school district has also spent  thousands of dollars for training and  Retreat to try to get along on taxpayers  dime despite the training fighting at  school board meetings and social media  continued so far unofficial results show  sapita and Ford may be losing their seat  as Cavazos may be keeping hers School  races are nonpartisan so any candidate  winning a majority of the vote will win  election to the board I reached out to  candidates today I was able to speak  with Irene Cepeda and Greg weeman  I think at the end of the day we trust  what the voters you know what the voters  say and uh that's you know that's that's  what we do as a democracy we we vote and  we change leadership or we need to um  according to the voters and I'm at peace  with that I'm what a relief I you know  it hurts a little uh you know you don't  like to lose any contest you're in if  you're a competitor  but at the same time it's uh to me it  was going to be an overwhelming  responsibility we have a lot of work  that needs to be done  the reminder these are unofficial  election results as all ballots are  still being counted and the remaining  trustees and candidates have not yet  responded to me at the time of this  report any new responses will be updated  online and on air reporting from CCSD  headquarters on Saharan Decatur Mary  Jane beliesa 8 News Now
 

